 (section federation
  (doc "Three phases, each independently shippable, each with pre-registered failure. FED1 implemented 2026-09-18; FED2 implemented 2026-10-01; FED3 re-opened 2026-10-13 (PP acted_by shipped; tuna half rehearsed live; PP half = bearer parity + the prims library).")
  (status in-progress)
  (subsection phases
   (status in-progress)
   (details
    (doc (|
      FED1 VALUE EXCHANGE (read-only, IMPLEMENTED 2026-09-18). GET
         /api/fed/value/:hash returns {hash, kind, payload} for either
         kind (tree ternary, bytes base64; a program hash resolves as
         its own ternary); the peer rehashes on receipt and trusts
         nothing but the hash (scripts/fed-pull.sh). Per-peer bearer
         identities via TUNA_FED_PEERS; hash-gated reads (byte-values
         law 2) mean no new authz model; fetches journal as op
         "fed-value" attributed to the calling identity.
      FED2 OPS-CHAIN SYNC (IMPLEMENTED 2026-10-01). Pull: GET
         /api/fed/ops?prefix=&after_seq= returns a contiguous op window;
         each row carries its true global predecessor hash so
         prefix-filtered (non-contiguous) windows verify per row
         (verify_window_rows; the d7e0ae7 lesson generalized - a window
         needs an anchor, which a carried prev_hash supplies for every
         row). Push: POST /api/fed/ops/apply re-verifies the window,
         rehashes inline values, checks per-peer authz (peer <name> ->
         ns/<name>/...; admin any), and folds it into the destination
         atomically. Append-only, no merge: a re-apply shadows under a
         fresh version; divergence is two namespaces, never silently
         reconciled.
      FED3 PRICKLYPEAR BRIDGE. Align attribution first (PP acted_by,
         still unshipped), then bearer parity (PP delegated Bearer ==
         tuna identity token), then a PP prims library calling
         /api/tree/* and /api/fed/* so PP rows and tuna paths cite each
         other by id/hash without either store encoding the other's
         internals. PP is a client of the tree surface before it is a
         peer of the chain. |))))
  (subsection pre-registered-failures
   (status implemented)
   (details
    (doc (|
      1. Two peers diverge on the same path and no check notices ->
         failure; divergence must surface as distinct namespaces or a
         verified rejection.  FED2 holds: ns/<peer>/ scoping keeps
         namespaces distinct, and a re-apply of an existing path
         SHADOWS under a fresh version (reported in the apply answer's
         "shadowed" list), never a silent merge.
      2. An applied op that fails rehash or chain-linkage verification
         -> failure; rejects are journaled, never absorbed.  FED2 holds:
         every pulled row carries its true prev_hash and apply
         re-verifies each row (tampered = 400, journaled fed-apply); a
         value-citing effect whose value is not held locally is also
         refused (400), value-pull-before-ops is the caller's law.
      3. A bridge write attributed to any identity other than the true
         actor (or its delegated identity) -> failure.  (FED3, not yet
         exercised.) |))))))

(* agent note (|2026-10-16 FED3 PROOFS WRAP-UP (board card
        todo/g4-fed3-proofs; answers PP run-primitive M12's NEXT line
        "allowlist, proofs?").  The structural proof is the journaling
        law itself: every fed-apply answer - applied, shadowed, refused,
        denied - is a journaled op row in the tree_ops chain (the apply
        answer's op_append, the deny paths' op_append), so a
        verification or attribution failure can never be absorbed
        silently; the chain IS the receipt, and F2's
        rejects-are-journaled clause holds at the same boundary.  Since
        M12 landed, the floor tightened on every side a bridge write
        could ride: g1 (2026-10-16) makes agent tree ops deny-all with
        explicit covering grants at the direct API too (the
        operator-side-door stance is retired); a2 (2026-10-16) makes
        fed apply authorize and verify the window BEFORE it writes, so
        a denied apply plants nothing; g2 (2026-10-16) adds per-runner
        revocable Bearer tokens (the glochid issue-token law) - the
        runner authenticates as its own identity at full bearer parity,
        which is exactly the attribution F3 demands.  WHAT PROOFS
        REMAIN: F3 is still "not yet exercised" by its own
        pre-registration - the one open obligation is an exercised
        attribution probe, positive (a bridge write through a runner
        token attributes to that identity: run rows carry caller,
        journal rows carry the actor, the ops chain carries the
        fed-apply row) and negative (any attempt to write outside
        ns/<peer>/ or through a revoked token is refused AND journaled,
        never absorbed).  Until that probe is pinned as a verify gate,
        F3 stays open by the MEASURE-don't-massage rule; the allowlist
        half of M12's question is answered on the tuna side by g1+g2
        (deny-all floor + per-runner allowlists are drivable end to
        end).|) *)
